IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lta-types`

-- Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK) — GOAL 1: REPAIR AND FITNESS (ss 9A,
-- 9B, 11, 13, 14).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1985-70.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — repair and fitness`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- "A period of n months beginning with" x ends on the day before the
-- corresponding date n months later, or on the last day of that month if it
-- has none.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

-- s 13(2) "(a) any part of the term which falls before the grant shall be
-- left out of account and the lease shall be treated as a lease for a term
-- commencing with the grant, (b) a lease which is determinable at the option
-- of the lessor before the expiration of seven years from the commencement of
-- the term shall be treated as a lease for a term of less than seven years,
-- and (c) a lease (other than a lease to which paragraph (b) applies) shall
-- not be treated as a lease for a term of less than seven years if it confers
-- on the lessee an option for renewal for a term which, together with the
-- original term, amounts to seven years or more." s 9B(8) is the same for
-- s 9A. A periodic tenancy has no term of seven years.
@ref ss 9B(8), 13(2)
GIVEN l IS A `Lease`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease is for a term of less than seven years` l IF
    BRANCH
        IF l's `periodic` THEN TRUE
        IF l's `determinable by the lessor within seven years` THEN TRUE
        IF l's `lessee's renewal option takes it to seven years or more` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE l's `term ends on` LESS THAN `the last day of the` 84 `months beginning with` (l's `granted on`)

GIVEN l IS A `Lease`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 14 exception applies to` l IF
    CONSIDER l's `section 14 exception`
    WHEN `no exception` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN l IS A `Lease`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease is within s 13(1A) or (1AA)` l IF
    CONSIDER l's `special tenancy`
    WHEN `a long secure tenancy under s 13(1A)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a long private registered provider tenancy under s 13(1AA)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 13(1) "Section 11 (repairing obligations) applies to a lease of a
-- dwelling-house granted on or after 24th October 1961 for a term of less
-- than seven years." (1A)-(1AA): also certain long social tenancies in
-- England. (1ZA): not a Welsh occupation contract. (1ZC): not an assured
-- tenancy of 7 years or more by a non-provider. s 14: the exceptions.
@ref ss 11(1), 13, 14
@export Whether the lessor's repairing covenant in s 11 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK) is implied in a lease: a lease of a dwelling-house granted on or after 24 October 1961 for a term of less than seven years (counted from the grant, with the s 13(2) rules), or a long social tenancy within s 13(1A)-(1AA) in England; not a Welsh occupation contract, not an assured tenancy within s 13(1ZC), and not within a s 14 exception. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Lease`  @desc The country, the dates and term of the lease, the kind of tenancy, and any exception
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11 applies to` l IF
        l's `a dwelling-house let wholly or mainly for human habitation`
    AND l's `granted on` AT LEAST Date 24 10 1961
    AND (   (`the lease is for a term of less than seven years` l AND NOT is1ZC)
         OR (`the lease is within s 13(1A) or (1AA)` l AND inEngland))
    AND NOT (l's `a Welsh occupation contract`)
    AND NOT (`a section 14 exception applies to` l)
    WHERE
        inEngland MEANS
            CONSIDER l's `country`
            WHEN `England` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        is1ZC MEANS
            CONSIDER l's `special tenancy`
            WHEN `an assured tenancy within s 13(1ZC)` THEN inEngland
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 9B(1) "Section 9A applies to a lease under which a dwelling is let wholly
-- or mainly for human habitation if either of the following applies— (a) the
-- lease is for a term of less than 7 years, or (b) the lease is of a kind
-- mentioned in subsection (1A), (1AA) or (1AB) of section 13". (2): not a
-- s 14 lease. (3)-(6): not a lease granted before the commencement date, or
-- under an earlier agreement or order, except an existing periodic or secure
-- tenancy, one arising on expiry of an earlier lease, or a fixed term renewed
-- on or after it.
@ref ss 9A(1), 9B(1)-(6)
@export Whether the covenant of fitness for human habitation in s 9A of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK) is implied in a lease of a dwelling in England: let wholly or mainly for human habitation, for a term of less than seven years or within s 13(1A)-(1AA), not within s 14, and granted on or after the commencement date (not under an earlier agreement or order), or an existing periodic or secure tenancy, one arising on expiry of an earlier lease, or a fixed term renewed on or after it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Lease`  @desc The country, the dates and term, the kind of tenancy, any exception, and how the lease stands to the commencement date of s 9A
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9A applies to` l IF
        inEngland
    AND l's `a dwelling-house let wholly or mainly for human habitation`
    AND (`the lease is for a term of less than seven years` l OR `the lease is within s 13(1A) or (1AA)` l)
    AND NOT (`a section 14 exception applies to` l)
    AND (   (    l's `granted on` AT LEAST l's `the commencement date of s 9A`
             AND NOT (l's `granted under an agreement or order made before 9A commenced`))
         OR l's `a periodic or secure tenancy in existence when 9A commenced`
         OR l's `arose on expiry of a lease granted before 9A commenced`
         OR l's `a fixed term renewed on or after 9A commenced`)
    WHERE
        inEngland MEANS
            CONSIDER l's `country`
            WHEN `England` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 9A(1)(a): fit "at the time the lease is granted". s 9B(4)(a): for a
-- periodic or secure tenancy in existence on the commencement date, "the
-- time that begins at the end of the period of 12 months beginning with the
-- commencement date" — the day after that period's last day. (The beginning
-- of the term is not an input; the grant is used.) s 9B(6): a renewal on or
-- after the commencement date "is to be treated as a grant of the lease on or
-- after that date", so the renewal date should be entered as `granted on`;
-- where the original, earlier grant is entered instead, the day is not known
-- and the answer is NOTHING (changed after the independent pass, F9).
@ref ss 9A(1), 9B(4)
@export The first day on which the covenant of fitness for human habitation in s 9A of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK) bites: the day the lease is granted; for a periodic or secure tenancy already in existence on the commencement date, the day after the end of the 12 months beginning with that date. NOTHING if s 9A does not apply, or for a s 9B(6) renewal entered with its original grant date (enter the renewal date as the grant). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Lease`  @desc The lease and the commencement date of s 9A
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first day the fitness covenant bites for` l MEANS
    IF   NOT (`section 9A applies to` l)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   l's `a periodic or secure tenancy in existence when 9A commenced`
         THEN JUST (`the day` 1 `days after` (`the last day of the` 12 `months beginning with` (l's `the commencement date of s 9A`)))
         ELSE IF   l's `a fixed term renewed on or after 9A commenced`
               AND l's `granted on` LESS THAN l's `the commencement date of s 9A`
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST (l's `granted on`)
